@RipMinner totally missed what AI in this article brings. Yes there have been advances reducing labor over the past 200 years (before as well but real acceleration now). The AI impact as described here makes all prior advancements infinitesimal. The world’s labor will be AI + robots. Man will need to do little in the operation of the world. What I used to call the Star Trek economy. There is no money, there is no need for it. All is provided. Heaven on earth 😂. 

The missing problem to all this is greed and religion, at least in the short term. The weak link in this new world is man. The killing, lying, greedy, cheating, selfish flesh machines aren’t being advanced as AI and an AI operated world is. 

AI will see that and ‘help’ man evolve those tendencies away. 😮
